---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | n8than.dev"
  description="A San Diego software engineer who ran a hospital's overnight cafeteria and built the ordering system its night shift used."
>
  <section class="container container--narrow">
    <h1 class="k-heading">About</h1>
    <blockquote class="epigraph">
      "Accept the things to which fate binds you, and love the people with whom fate brings you
      together, and do so with all your heart."
      <cite>— Marcus Aurelius</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      I'm a developer based in San Diego. CS degree from San Diego State (2020), then a pivot to
      hospital food service at Scripps Mercy during COVID. I ran the overnight cafeteria solo,
      cooking for 50+ staff at a full inner-city hospital. The more care I put into it, the more
      people showed up. The night shift left a wall of{' '}
      <a href="/recognition">thank-you notes</a>, and the work earned Scripps Health's 2025 Values
      in Action Award. Wait times and volume became a real problem I could actually solve.
    </p>
    <p>
      Through 2025 I built CafeNightClub, a food ordering system for 80+ hospital staff, and ran it
      in production into early 2026. Staff could order from their floor and pick up when it was
      ready, no more waiting around. Since then I've been building for other people's floors too.
      Build Sheet Studio, for Solid Woodworx, turns a Shopify order into the printable build sheet a
      CNC shop actually works from. In fall 2026 I built a staff web app inside a client's own
      platform: TypeScript on Cloudflare Workers, reading live orders from their store. It was
      merged into their production codebase that September. Claude Code made the whole process
      faster.
    </p>
    <p>
      I want to build for healthcare, infrastructure, and the systems that hold communities
      together. Sympatheia: the idea that we're all connected and responsible for one another.
      That's what drives the work. This portfolio and the projects in it are where that starts.
    </p>

    <section class="skills">
      <h2 class="k-subheading">Technical skills</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Languages</dt>
        <dd>JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, SQL, HTML, CSS</dd>
        <dt>Frontend</dt>
        <dd>React, Next.js, Astro, Tailwind CSS, DaisyUI, SSR, Responsive Design, Accessibility</dd>
        <dt>Backend</dt>
        <dd>
          Node.js, Bun, PostgreSQL, SQLite, Drizzle ORM, Supabase, better-auth, RESTful APIs, SSE,
          Docker, Linux (Ubuntu), Caddy, PM2, Hetzner
        </dd>
        <dt>Tools &amp; Practices</dt>
        <dd>
          Git, GitHub, CI/CD (GitHub Actions), Vitest, AI-augmented development (Claude), State
          Management, Database Design
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="education">
      <h2 class="k-subheading">Education</h2>
      <div class="degree">
        <p class="school">San Diego State University</p>
        <p class="program">Bachelor of Science in Computer Science</p>
        <time class="year">2020</time>
      </div>
      <div class="degree">
        <p class="school">Grossmont College</p>
        <p class="program">Associate of Science in Mathematics / Computer Science</p>
        <time class="year">2017</time>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="links">
      <h2 class="k-subheading">Find me online</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            class="k-btn"
            href="https://github.com/Nyx000"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            class="k-btn"
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sd-nhuse/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
          >
        </li>
        <li><a class="k-btn" href="mailto:husenathan@gmail.com">Email</a></li>
        <li>
          <a class="k-btn" href="/resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Résumé<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .epigraph {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .epigraph cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  /* In-text links need more than colour to stand apart from the prose (WCAG 1.4.1). */
  p a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .links {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .k-heading,
  .k-subheading {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .links ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .skills {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .skills dl {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .skills dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .skills dt:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .skills dd {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0 0;
  }

  .education {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .degree {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .school {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .program {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .year {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>
